WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.188
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:09.002
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:14.915
Unit nine: Describing a Process. Today you will explain how something is done step by step.

4
00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.925
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:21.902
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.751
Process.

7
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.051
Process means a series of steps.

8
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.533
Describe the process clearly.

9
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.814
Your turn. Say: Process.

10
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:36.691
Process.

11
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.405
Step.

12
00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:41.846
Step means one stage in a process.

13
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.008
The first step is easy.

14
00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:46.944
Your turn. Say: Step.

15
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.604
Step.

16
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.189
Firstly.

17
00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:55.276
Firstly means used for the first step.

18
00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:57.883
Firstly, wash the rice.

19
00:00:58.483 --> 00:01:01.066
Your turn. Say: Firstly.

20
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:04.797
Firstly.

21
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.714
Afterwards.

22
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:10.065
Afterwards means later, after something.

23
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.243
Afterwards, add the water.

24
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.653
Your turn. Say: Afterwards.

25
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.606
Afterwards.

26
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:21.084
Finally.

27
00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:24.396
Finally means used for the last step.

28
00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:26.646
Finally, serve the dish.

29
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.426
Your turn. Say: Finally.

30
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.140
Finally.

31
00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:34.745
Passive.

32
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.166
Passive means a verb form: be plus past participle.

33
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.506
Use the passive voice.

34
00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:44.804
Your turn. Say: Passive.

35
00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:48.621
Passive.

36
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:50.384
Ingredient.

37
00:01:51.383 --> 00:01:53.940
Ingredient means one food in a recipe.

38
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.120
Rice is the main ingredient.

39
00:01:56.717 --> 00:01:58.870
Your turn. Say: Ingredient.

40
00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:02.688
Ingredient.

41
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.660
Instruction.

42
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.439
Instruction means words that tell you what to do.

43
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.678
Read the instructions.

44
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:14.145
Your turn. Say: Instruction.

45
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.164
Instruction.

46
00:02:18.967 --> 00:02:22.432
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:25.643
Visal, how do I explain a process?

48
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:35.265
Use time words in order: firstly, next, then, afterwards, finally. Each sentence describes one step.

49
00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:37.781
Should I use the passive?

50
00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:47.204
Yes, often. The rice is washed, then it is boiled. The passive focuses on the action, not the person.

51
00:02:48.317 --> 00:02:49.933
What about instructions?

52
00:02:51.017 --> 00:02:58.232
For instructions, use the imperative: wash the rice, add water. It is short and direct.

53
00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:00.937
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.783 --> 00:03:05.048
Grammar focus: Passive voice for a process.

55
00:03:05.348 --> 00:03:06.512
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.217 --> 00:03:09.216
The rice is washed in clean water.

57
00:03:10.117 --> 00:03:12.685
The vegetables are cut into small pieces.

58
00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:19.464
Use the passive, is or are plus the past participle, when the action is more important than the person.

59
00:03:20.217 --> 00:03:23.670
Be careful! Don't say: The rice washed in water.

60
00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:27.575
Say: The rice is washed in water.

61
00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:29.155
Passive needs be.

62
00:03:29.967 --> 00:03:32.596
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.773
How to Cook Rice.

64
00:03:35.073 --> 00:03:37.827
Firstly, the rice is washed in clean water.

65
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:41.390
Next, it is put into a pot with water.

66
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.922
Then the pot is heated for fifteen minutes.

67
00:03:45.933 --> 00:03:48.223
Afterwards, the rice is left to rest.

68
00:03:49.233 --> 00:03:51.895
Finally, it is served hot with vegetables.

69
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.955
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:57.817 --> 00:03:59.735
A process is a series of blank.

71
00:04:00.035 --> 00:04:03.526
A, steps. B, jokes. C, rooms.

72
00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:08.927
The answer is A: steps.

73
00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.886
Firstly shows the blank step.

74
00:04:12.186 --> 00:04:15.282
A, only. B, first. C, last.

75
00:04:18.833 --> 00:04:20.612
The answer is B: first.

76
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.982
The passive is be plus the past blank.

77
00:04:24.282 --> 00:04:27.877
A, noun. B, name. C, participle.

78
00:04:31.433 --> 00:04:33.944
The answer is C: participle.

79
00:04:35.083 --> 00:04:36.874
Instructions use the blank.

80
00:04:37.174 --> 00:04:40.676
A, imperative. B, future. C, question.

81
00:04:44.233 --> 00:04:46.094
The answer is A: imperative.

82
00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.913
The rice is served blank.

83
00:04:49.213 --> 00:04:52.599
A, never. B, hot. C, cold.

84
00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:57.819
The answer is B: hot.

85
00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:02.173
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:03.017 --> 00:05:04.912
How do you describe a process?

87
00:05:13.717 --> 00:05:15.263
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:15.563 --> 00:05:28.934
I use time words in order: firstly, next, then and finally. I often use the passive, for example the rice is washed. Each sentence gives one clear step.

89
00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:30.839
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:36.411
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive voice for a process.

91
00:05:36.711 --> 00:05:40.791
Today's value is thoroughness. Do the whole job, and do it well.

92
00:05:41.091 --> 00:05:43.488
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

93
00:05:43.788 --> 00:05:46.324
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

